# Svalbard offline drive

You run from a Svalbard USB drive. There is no internet. Do not try curl, wget, git clone, pip install, npm install or any other download. They fail.

The drive has an offline library: reference archives, SQLite databases and maps. For a factual question, look it up with the `svalbard` tools instead of guessing:

1. `vault_sources` lists what is on the drive. Call it first.
2. `search` finds articles by keyword.
3. `search_read` reads one article. Pass the `source` and `path` from a search result.

To build something (an app, dashboard, map, document, firmware), first read a procedure: with no search index, list `skills/` and read the fitting SKILL.md. Use only the libraries and tools it names; they are on this drive. Pack HTML with `svalbard-drive html pack`; never link a CDN.

Rules:

- Name the source you used.
- If the drive has no answer, say so. Do not invent one.
- Do not repeat a tool call with the same arguments. If it failed twice, stop and tell the user.
- `./run` on the drive is an interactive menu for the user. Do not run it.
